AB  - The electronic health record (EHR) system has the potential to convert the healthcare industry from a typically paper-based industry to one that exploits medical and other types of data to help providers in providing high-quality care to patients. Recently, artificial intelligence (AI) has converted numerous industries, and health care is at the lead of this innovation. Conventional risk stratification models are frequently based on structured data and simple statistical methods that may capture subtle patterns in complex clinical datasets. The advent of the Generative Pre-trained Transformer (GPT) technique offers a promising alternative, combining innovative natural language processing (NLP) capabilities to understand both structured and unstructured data. GPT systems excel at perception and the generation of human-like text, enabling them to extract valuable insights from medical notes, EHRs, and patient histories. This paper proposes a Prognosis Analysis of Electronic Health Records Using Transformer Neural Network and Feature Engineering Techniques (PAEHR-TNNFET) approach. The main aim of the PAEHR-TNNFET approach is to leverage AI, driven by GPT, to analyse EHRs and extract meaningful clinical insights to improve decision-making and patient care. At first, the data pre-processing stage contains data normalisation, categorical encoding, handling missing values, and outlier detection to normalise the input data. Furthermore, the feature selection process includes variance threshold (VT), Chi-Square, analysis of variance (ANOVA), mutual information (MI), Least Absolute Shrinkage and Selection Operator (LASSO), and recursive feature elimination (RFE) to select the most significant features from the dataset. At last, the PAEHR-TNNFET model implements the transformer neural network (TNN), a GPT-based classifier. The comparison analysis of the PAEHR-TNNFET model showed superior accuracy of 98.51 % compared to other methods on the SymbiPredict dataset.
