AB  - Object detection in remote sensing images is key to applications like environmental protection and disaster monitoring. DEtection TRansformer (DETR)-based methods have recently gained increasing attention in remote sensing object detection but still face challenges in such scenarios: the low discriminability of aerial targets and the difficulty in learning representations that integrate both semantic and geometric clues for oriented object detection. To address these challenges, we propose Rotation and Semantic Co-aware DEtection TRansformer (RS-DETR). Within RS-DETR, we propose a Rotational and Semantic Co-Attention (RSCA) mechanism in the decoder. RSCA employs dual-branch learning to effectively capture heterogeneous geometric and semantic features, leading to accurate oriented localization and classification. In addition, we develop an Adaptive Context-Aggregated Feature Enhancement (ACA-FE) module to dynamically aggregate context clues, improving the discriminability of challenging targets. Moreover, to accelerate training convergence, we reformulate DETR’s Hungarian matching cost and loss function by incorporating an object mask constraint. Extensive experiments across three benchmark datasets demonstrate that RS-DETR achieves state-of-the-art performance in remote sensing object detection.
