AB  - In the coal conveying pipeline of thermal power plant, the silica in the pulverized coal would accelerate the wear of equipment and affect the combustion efficiency. The particle size of pulverized coal is also related to combustion efficiency and economic benefits. At present, the detection of coal particle size and impurity silica mainly relying on manual sampling and laboratory analysis, such as laser particle size analyzing and microscopic method. These methods are not only time-consuming, but also difficult to achieve continuous observation the input of combustion materials. Therefore, this paper proposes an image detection method based on improved U-Net, which can detect the pulverized coal and impurity silica in the pipeline. Improvements have been made to U-Net, mainly reflected in the encoder part of U-Net is replaced by the Residual Network with 50 layers (ResNet50), and Bidirectional Feature Pyramid Network (BiFPN) and Squeeze and Excitation Network (SENet) are integrated after it. In addition, the combination of transposed convolution and Convolutional Block Attention Module (CBAM) is adopted in the decoder part. Combined with actual working conditions, the network is lightweighted by replacing the ordinary convolutions in encoder and decoder with depthwise separable convolution and dilated convolution, achieving a goal of lightweight computing. The experimental results show that the value of Mean Intersection over Union (MIoU) is 81.93%, Mean Pixel Accuracy (MPa) is 89.36%, Mean Precision (MPr) is 88.71%, parameters is 61.63 Mega, the Giga Floating-point Operations Per Second (GFLOPS) is 110.41 and Frame per Second (FPS) is 50.67. The error of pulverized coal is less than 4%.
