AB  - Photorealistic image generation is a vital technique to produce digital images, which convert the source domain into the target image through a powerful tool, namely, the Generative Adversarial Network. However, the conventional GAN possessed the drawbacks of unstable training, mismatched images, and model collapse. Therefore, to tackle these constraints, the Triplex Attention enabled Diffusion Generative Adversarial Network (TriADGAN) is introduced to produce high-resolution photorealistic images from both text and images. The TriADGAN utilizes triplex attention to learn significant features of the images with minimum computational resources while handling the intricate structure. Furthermore, the attention helps the model to minimize the redundancy, thereby improving the training stability and generalizability of the model. Additionally, the TriADGAN includes weighted heterogeneous graph-based text embedding to conserve the optimal features of the text, which upgrades the standard of the text description. Hence, the inclusion of these advanced techniques exhibits the TriADGAN to attain exceptional performance in terms of a Fréchet inception distance, Correlation coefficient, Structural Similarity Index, and Peak Signal-to-Noise Ratio of 5.08, 0.85, 0.91, 38.37 dB, and 4.87, 0.82, 0.94, 39.57 dB, for text-to-image and image-to-image generation, respectively.
