KW  - Malicious uniform resource locators
KW  - Feature classification
KW  - Bahdanau attention mechanism
KW  - eXplainable artificial intelligence
KW  - Recurrent neural network
AB  - In the era of rapidly expanding web content, accurately distinguishing between legitimate and malicious Uniform Resource Locators (URLs) remains a persistent cybersecurity challenge. While several recent studies have explored multiclass URL classification across benign, phishing, malware, and defacement categories, many existing approaches rely on heavy pre-training or lack interpretability and scalability. This paper presents DeepURLGuard, an interpretable and resource-efficient deep learning framework that integrates lexical, content, and network-based features through Particle Swarm Optimization (PSO)-driven feature selection. The model employs a Bidirectional Recurrent Neural Network (Bi-RNN) with a modified attention mechanism and gradient clipping to enhance stability and performance. Explainable AI (XAI) techniques further ensure transparency by elucidating the influence of individual features on classification decisions. Evaluated on a dataset of 296,983 URLs, DeepURLGuard achieves 95 % accuracy in multiclass detection, demonstrating competitive performance against state-of-the-art baselines. The framework effectively balances accuracy, interpretability, and computational efficiency, offering a practical and scalable solution for real-world malicious URL analysis.
